                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8dfd0e10-acee-345e-9855-59df4dd8c3cf",
                        "entry_id": "769a118d-a3c5-3b64-b09b-4960a41e7a5b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар., разг. то же, что листать; переворачивать листы (книги, рукописи, тетради и т. п.)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "95b5524d-0bfd-451a-a923-7074feb2a946",
                                "sense_id": "8dfd0e10-acee-345e-9855-59df4dd8c3cf",
                                "text": "Максим Кузьмич садится на его место, раскрывает дело и листует; Тарелкин ему указывает, разговор идет вполголоса."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea6c7d22-6196-48dc-b538-5dd61d87c6a1",
                                "sense_id": "8dfd0e10-acee-345e-9855-59df4dd8c3cf",
                                "text": "― А пускай копаются, ― сказал профсоюзник, ― дай им старые архивы листовать, тебе-то што?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "99f4a510-d016-4f7a-a7d6-0dbb08767087",
                        "source_entry_id": "769a118d-a3c5-3b64-b09b-4960a41e7a5b",
                        "source_sense_id": "8dfd0e10-acee-345e-9855-59df4dd8c3cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "turn over",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "turn over",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9cd0cc9-1005-3ea8-a997-ef65929ada3c",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see turn, over."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c13a19c1-3c9c-4117-b9a4-5e44c4e008e9",
                                                "sense_id": "d9cd0cc9-1005-3ea8-a997-ef65929ada3c",
                                                "text": "The family feeling was intensified as we stopped to speak to mothers in the cottage gardens, or waved to distant tractors turning over chocolate-brown furrows and driven by 'my dad' or 'my Uncle Bob'."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c601b6de-865a-3027-b64d-3068859b5524",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To flip over; to rotate uppermost to bottom."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc541dbe-1590-46ea-a7f5-4cad57373e51",
                                                "sense_id": "c601b6de-865a-3027-b64d-3068859b5524",
                                                "text": "Turn over the box and look at the bottom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e3ca753-639f-40f8-9aaa-b47722af32f2",
                                                "sense_id": "c601b6de-865a-3027-b64d-3068859b5524",
                                                "text": "The brakes were applied immediately, but the engine ran into a sand drag at approximately 20 m.p.h., plunged down the embankment, and turned over on its side at the bottom."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4aee2c21-470a-3a5f-8726-571a937b3bb3",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To relinquish; give back."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3320888-a884-43b2-8842-9b9f2745b774",
                                                "sense_id": "4aee2c21-470a-3a5f-8726-571a937b3bb3",
                                                "text": "They turned over the evidence to the authorities."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f86eeb8e-54b5-3377-8267-9466e7c6c2fe",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To transfer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65f628d1-54e2-490b-ad4b-d43306df6c39",
                                                "sense_id": "f86eeb8e-54b5-3377-8267-9466e7c6c2fe",
                                                "text": "But what is to be done with our manufacturing population […] This one thing, of doing for them by ‘underselling all people,’ and filling our own bursten pockets and appetites by the road; and turning over all care for any ‘population,’ or human or divine consideration except cash only, to the winds, with a “Laissez-faire” and the rest of it: this is evidently not the thing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f016351f-b7d6-34c2-890d-c032a8052282",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To produce, complete, or cycle through."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5961d3a-4b9b-49c2-aaff-4ed7f702d8a5",
                                                "sense_id": "f016351f-b7d6-34c2-890d-c032a8052282",
                                                "text": "They can turn over about three hundred units per hour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "00c7a62d-35ab-321b-b0a1-471c8627733a",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To generate (a certain amount of money from sales)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f05fe5af-09a2-441e-9b93-2b3954ec8f78",
                                                "sense_id": "00c7a62d-35ab-321b-b0a1-471c8627733a",
                                                "text": "The business turned over £1m last year."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63b58d5d-992f-34cd-ad59-6fef2d6a5c82",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mull, ponder"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45326ce2-059f-4cf6-9926-7e4c5aee678e",
                                                "sense_id": "63b58d5d-992f-34cd-ad59-6fef2d6a5c82",
                                                "text": "Thus they dwelled for nearly a year, and in that time Robin Hood often turned over in his mind many means of making an even score with the Sheriff"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "797cbb7e-6622-3cd9-bbbd-013b0770b261",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spin the crankshaft of an internal combustion engine using the starter or hand crank in an attempt to make it run."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f6184af-a765-3a7f-a4a7-92a981854f79",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To give up control (of the ball and thus the ability to score)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "faf81cc6-249f-42e9-a562-730cd9639aba",
                                                "sense_id": "3f6184af-a765-3a7f-a4a7-92a981854f79",
                                                "text": "The Giants didn't turn the ball over in their last four games."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2268291e-2e3b-330c-a850-8364d350cad5",
                                        "entry_id": "1cc30e3f-9d0e-33d4-86a2-0ed840600b5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cause extensive disturbance or disruption to (a room, storage place, etc.), e.g. while searching for an item, or ransacking a property."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "211dfb9e-84a8-4b56-a599-c519df1979fb",
                                                "sense_id": "2268291e-2e3b-330c-a850-8364d350cad5",
                                                "text": "I've turned over the whole place, but I still can't find my glasses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b52bd1cc-f7b2-4b64-be76-bdebc9e19722",
                                                "sense_id": "2268291e-2e3b-330c-a850-8364d350cad5",
                                                "text": "Thieves turned over the apartment while the owners were away on holiday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9beb1a4b-5003-4c94-9ab1-daa07b1ad5d7",
                        "source_entry_id": "769a118d-a3c5-3b64-b09b-4960a41e7a5b",
                        "source_sense_id": "8dfd0e10-acee-345e-9855-59df4dd8c3cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "leaf",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "leaf",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9ba30db-2b3d-3ef5-91b4-b7c38df00e16",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The usually green and flat organ that represents the most prominent feature of most vegetative plants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be57f66c-16eb-411c-9b1e-b3182d9f6aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "e9ba30db-2b3d-3ef5-91b4-b7c38df00e16",
                                                "text": "Earless ghost swift moths become “invisible” to echolocating bats by forming mating clusters close (less than half a meter) above vegetation and effectively blending into the clutter of echoes that the bat receives from the leaves and stems around them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b7d5d57-af7d-3ba8-b0e9-246a19893488",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A foliage leaf or any of the many and often considerably different structures it can specialise into."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07d12a95-91e0-3bc7-a60c-bfa8aa17461f",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything resembling the leaf of a plant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82e58b66-47c2-31cb-aeac-ae31b05cdbbc",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sheet of a book, magazine, etc. (consisting of two pages, one on each face of the leaf)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ddf17e9-9fb2-4759-a35d-f1e73f1fd6d0",
                                                "sense_id": "82e58b66-47c2-31cb-aeac-ae31b05cdbbc",
                                                "text": "Heretofore advertisers have had to buy and pay for a leaf — two pages."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6bc4ec29-cedd-3ff5-bdef-5de75b4d4659",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sheet of any substance beaten or rolled until very thin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9cfcbaf-7e0a-46f7-95f0-58bb815768b0",
                                                "sense_id": "6bc4ec29-cedd-3ff5-bdef-5de75b4d4659",
                                                "text": "gold leaf"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56211ac1-0e92-3899-82b2-79f90e13f9bb",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of the individual flat or curved strips of metal, typically made of spring steel, that make up a leaf spring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fff22b9b-1100-4819-a5af-6a5105218195",
                                                "sense_id": "56211ac1-0e92-3899-82b2-79f90e13f9bb",
                                                "text": "Lumbering down a precipitous \"slideway,\" the Thornycroft broke two main leaves in the back spring[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aae5e7f2-e7e2-3707-9b2e-a56c9af6591e",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tea leaves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "in-plural",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f84a095-5228-34b7-8e1d-a0741c789080",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A flat section used to extend the size of a table."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A moveable panel, e.g. of a bridge or door, originally one that hinged but now also applied to other forms of movement."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b0b379e-3933-414c-9b9c-024e3e700af2",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "The train car has one single-leaf and two double-leaf doors per side."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88e843cb-a12d-40a7-89b7-ecfeb34105ab",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "The bridge shear locks were repaired and the long ends of the shear locks shortened about two inches to eliminate butting of the bridge leafs against each other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "585147bb-5a80-4efb-9797-9424defc9af1",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "It will be noted that the pivotal mounting of the cylinders is such that the cylinders have their greatest leverage (i.e., exert the greatest door-opening force) when the door leafs 24, 28 are closed because the cylinders are generally perpendicular to the closed leafs. This is desirable because the load on the leafs is the greatest when they are closed due to air pressure. As the leafs begin to open and this air pressure decreases, the opening force exerted by the cylinders on the door leafs decreases and the opening speed of the leafs increases."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08115de0-c803-4013-811a-0c631988af28",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "THE NTSB RECOMMENDS THAT THE U.S. COAST GUARD: REQUIRE OWNERS/OPERATORS OF BASCULE BRIDGES TO INSTALL CAUTION LIGHTS AND DAYLIGHT MARKINGS AT ELEVATION POINTS ON BRIDGE LEAFS WHERE THEY PROTRUDE OVER NAVIGABLE CHANNELS TO IDEN TIFY^([sic]) TO MARINERS THE POINT AT WHICH FULL SKYWARD CHANNEL CLEARANCE IS NOT AVAILABLE TO TRANSITING VESSELS: THE LIGHTS SHOULD ACTIVATE WHEN THE BRIDGELEAFS ARE IN THE NORMAL FULLY OPEN POSITION.[…]THE NTSB RECOMMENDS THAT THE U.S. COAST GUARD: REQUIRE THAT BRIDGE OWNERS/OPERATORS PROVIDE IN BASCULE BRIDGE PERMIT APPLICATIONS THE ANGLE OF THE BRIDGELEAF(S). THE MAXIMUM VERTICAL CLEARANCE AT THE FENDERS AND AT THE BRIDGELEAF ENDS, AND THE EXTENT OF HORIZONTAL CHANNEL CLEARANCE OVER WHICH FULL SKYWARD CLEARANCE IS AVAILABLE WHEN THE BRIDGE LEAFS ARE IN THE FULLY OPEN POSITION."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "541f5be5-df92-4093-a8af-8fb887e63b84",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "The four separate segments of the movable bridge span, known as bridge leafs, were alternately rehabilitated while maintaining upper-level roadway and pedestrian traffic on one-half of the bridge and waterway traffic on one-half of the river channel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "706204b7-67c8-43d0-8ecd-ef29a2d1f549",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "The hydraulic system lifts and rotates two 413-ft (126-m) bridge leafs, each weighing 7,500 tons, in just four minutes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8c8d8f2-a137-4e51-b582-e3cb9210330d",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "Note the Art Deco-style sculptures on the wall of the bridge house showing a ship passing under the raised bridge leafs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcc385db-1684-4c1f-9867-8b807f725a47",
                                                "sense_id": "503de5d6-beba-39c0-b30b-45d7b2343b93",
                                                "text": "Like I’ve said, John, you’ve got to get the two bridge leafs to come down very slowly to a complete stop in order to trigger the tongue locks. This is what holds the two leafs of the bridge firmly in place. Otherwise, the bridge leafs will start bouncing, and once they start bouncing, you’ll never stop them from goin’ straight up in the air."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3854224e-a019-36ee-b7d1-38ac25836f44",
                                        "entry_id": "b38c6d0d-f94d-3a3b-ac76-a6774a49195e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a tree, a node that has no descendants."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
